 "state": "predicted-static; import only after live capture confirms the key (validate_predicted.py confirm + gate on the AQ-01/AQ-03 Stage 2 capture)",
 "created_at_utc": "2026-11-13T21:49:37.786953+00:00",
 "method": "W7-STAGE2 F1 detail pass (w2-effects v2 method adapted to the Stage 2 luminance fields; lane-s2, claude-einhander).\n\nKeys: AD934A7E-FC338604 (flames), 3DD37B6B-AFAD5A36 (dark additive smoke), 4915FBCF-056E3BD0 (glow).  All three CLUTs are\nSTP (additive) wherever visible.  Base = the frozen stage2-opening-fx-v1 export of the same key (prep-v1 / fx-v1 index\nmaster render, cell-isolated, luminance-field RGB, class map exact at every native texel centre).\n\n  guides  per drawn cell: native luminance field Lb (normalised convolution of the CLUT luminance of the visible native\n          texels, gaussian 0.55 texel, texel-centred bilinear 8x upsample) -> guide colour = hue-smoothed CLUT colour of Lb\n          (flame, glow) or neutral grey (smoke) times a gain that lifts the CLUT's brightest entry to ~230; alpha-0 = black.\n          Cells are placed 1:1 on the 8x master grid (glow at 16x, boxed down by 2 after generation) on SDXL-bucket canvases.\n  gen     JuggernautXL v9 img2img (core nodes; denoise 0.6, cfg 6, 32 steps, dpmpp_2m karras; w2-effects v2 parameters),\n          inside gpu_slot('lane-s2', <= 10 min) after the nvidia-smi health check.\n  build   AI luminance / gain = La (inverse ramp: the guide is luminance-exact, so the inverse is a division).\n          Low frequencies locked to native: Ln = La + G(Lb - La, 1.6 texel); band limit G(0.7 px) (motion);\n          weight = native visibility of the cell (dilated 1 texel, feathered 0.6 texel); outside it Lb.\n          Flames only (core_pin): where Lb is within 4-14 lum of the CLUT's brightest entry, Ln is pulled up to max(Ln, Lb)\n          (weight ramps 0 -> 1), so the native white-hot plateau stays white and the AI licks live around it.\n          Colour = CLUT ramp at Ln (Ramp: visible entries sorted by luminance, entry chroma smoothed over entries within\n          ~6 lum units, brightest entry exact, linear interpolation; below the darkest entry the colour fades linearly\n          to black; r1/r2 guides were rendered with an earlier per-pixel gaussian ramp, which only tints the guide), faded to the v1\n          colour within 1.25 texels of the CLUT's alpha cut; per-cell light energy locked to 0.95-1.05 of native (scalar).\n  export  alpha = the v1 class plane, bit-identical; class re-validated at every native texel centre; pixels outside\n          every drawn cell = v1 exactly.\nusage: python -I f1_detail.py guides|gen|build <run> [job names]",
 "supersedes": "stage2-opening-fx-v1 RGB of AD934A7E-FC338604, 3DD37B6B-AFAD5A36 and 4915FBCF-056E3BD0 only (alpha planes bit-identical to v1). The other four fx-v1 keys (AD934A7E-B949240B, 4915FBCF-3A9D7113 / ADB1BC56 / B949240B: debris, rubble, panels) stay in stage2-opening-fx-v1.",
